        name: `Jason DeCristofaro Trio with Special Guest Wendy Jones`,
        sort_time: "2026-01-07 19:00:00",
        end_time_formatted: "2026-01-07 23:59",
        detail: "Jason DeCristofaro Trio with Special Guest Wendy Jones Thu, Jan 07 Join us Thursday Night for an ensemble described as electric from their earliest collaboration. The Jason DeCristofaro Trio brings an uncommon chemistry and spontaneity to the jazz stage. Rooted in the jazz tradition but guided by the instincts of the moment, the trio creates a thrilling musical conversation through inventive improvisation and fresh interpretations of both classic jazz standards and original compositions. \n \n Joined by vocalist Wendy Jones , whose expressive voice and deeply personal approach have earned critical acclaim, the ensemble brings her gift for musical storytelling and finding beauty and fresh meaning in the songs she interprets. \n \n Together, they offer an evening of sophisticated, heartfelt jazz that is as engaging and unpredictable as it is memorable. \n \n Featured Musicians \n Jason DeCristofaro -Vibraphone \n Rick Dilling - Drums \n Kevin Kehrberg - Bass \n Wendy Jones -Special Guest Vocalist \n \n About Jason DeCristofaro \n Dr. Jason DeCristofaro is an active music educator, multi-instrumentalist, and composer/arranger based in Asheville, NC. Entering his 10th year at Warren Wilson College, he currently serves as Assistant Professor of Music, Chair of the Music Department, and Director of the Kittredge Arts Center. Jason\'s classical and jazz music has been performed internationally and throughout the United States, and his compositions are published with C. Alan, Per-Mus, and Tapspace. Best known as a jazz vibraphonist, Jason was the winner of the 2011 Yamaha/Percussive Arts Society Terry Gibbs Competition and has performed on national and global stages with Randy Brecker, Dr. Sam Waymon (Nina Simone\'s brother), Jocelyn Gould, and Sharel Cassity. \n \n $10/Door. Reserve Your Table Here for Guaranteed Seating! \n Read More 07:00 PM SHOW 08:30 PM SHOW",
