        end_time: "?",
        name: `Dirty Logic Presents: Babylon Brothers | The Music of Steely Dan, Reimagined for Jazz Quintet`,
        sort_time: "2026-01-15 19:00:00",
        end_time_formatted: "2026-01-15 23:59",
        detail: "Dirty Logic Presents: Babylon Brothers | The Music of Steely Dan, Reimagined for Jazz Quintet Fri, Jan 15 Dirty Logic Presents: Babylon Brothers | The Music of Steely Dan, Reimagined for Jazz Quintet \n \n Dirty Logic is known across the Southeast for their faithful, inspired performances of the Steely Dan catalog, playing sold-out theaters with eleven musicians on stage. \n \n This show is something different . For one night only , Dirty Logic’s rhythm section comes to Hotel Eve to play these songs as an instrumental jazz quintet. Every song stays rooted in the originals you know and love, with the familiar melodies, grooves, and changes. From there, the band opens each one up with fresh instrumental interpretations and improvisation, bringing the songs to life in a new and unique way that only these players can. Underneath the studio polish, Becker and Fagen were deeply rooted in jazz, and this show celebrates that side of their music. \n \n If you love Dirty Logic, this is a rare chance to hear the players who drive that band up close, in an intimate jazz club setting. \n \n Featuring: \n Jonathan Cole, tenor saxophone \n Duane Simpson, guitar \n Alex Taub, keys \n Jake Wolf, bass \n Patrick Armitage, drums \n \n $25/Advance. Seating is limited, Reserve Early! \n \n \n Read More 07:00 PM SHOW 09:00 PM SHOW",
