        end_time_formatted: "2026-12-08 23:59",
        detail: "What started as a 70th birthday celebration for Gregg Allman in 2017 evolved into an annual celebration of one of rock ‘n’ roll’s finest catalogs. Galvanizing the families of Allman & Betts: The Allman Betts Family Revival has become a yearly tradition featuring some of the finest musicians on the planet.\nSons Devon Allman and Duane Betts honor their families\' legacies with legends Robert Randolph, Judith Hill, Andy Frasco, Luther Dickinson, Jimmy Hall, Steel Beans, Larry McCray, Cody Dickinson, Alex Orbison, and Abby Stahlschmidt. \nTo celebrate a DECADE of The Allman Betts Family Revival the first set of the show will honor the original lineup and focus on songs from the 1970s. The second set will recapture the electricity of the 1990s era by focusing on songs from the Allman Brothers’ renaissance.",
